  {
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "> I think this issue should be reported to triton\n\ncould be.\nor it could be that torch has a specialized kernel for converting float8 to other dtypes for devices that don't natively support float8, implemented via bit manipulation. Then it would be reasonable for Triton to say it this isn't a bug on their part (dtype not supported), but it would be one of torch (assuming the goal of torch.compile is to be able to compile all GPU code).\n\nI don't know which one it is.\n",
