  {
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "@drisspg As we're here, let me ask: Do you think it's ok to let TorchInductor generate some inline PTX or some Triton bit packing ops, rather than the Triton op `cast`, on GPUs with sm < 89, as suggested in https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/8929#issuecomment-3625376340 ?\n\nThere are many ways to implement this, such as in Triton, or in PyTorch, or a new package like FlagGems or Liger Kernel. I just patched Triton and do this on my computer without problem (and many users of triton-windows are doing this). The problem is to find a way that makes it easy for more users.",
    "created_at": "2025-12-14T11:01:02Z",
